+    the test's own clause check, rerun it with that guard switched off by
+    overlay so the test's own line must catch it; keep the guarded run as the
+    realistic result (901a auditor 3).
+12. **A path-traversal test can be unable to fail.** When the guarded path is
+    `<dir>/<prefix>.<id>`, an `../../evil` id makes `<prefix>.` a missing
+    folder, so the OS refuses the path even with the sanitizer deleted. Create
+    the first component the hostile id names (`mkdir <dir>/<prefix>.x`, id
+    `x/../../evil`) and assert nothing lands outside `<dir>`; then delete the
+    sanitizer and watch the test fail. (2026-10-23: `~/.claude/hooks` gate
+    tests passed with sanitization removed.)
+13. **A mutant that doesn't build is not a kill.** Removing the only use of an
+    import (or a variable), or adding a call (`time.Sleep`) without its import,
+    makes the package fail to compile, so the "failing" test never ran; count
+    a kill only on the test's own `--- FAIL` line (in table subtests sharing one
+    fixture, read the first failing case: one mutant's write fails every later
+    case too; 86bcm927y auditor 3). Keep the import used (e.g. `OneLine(text) + html.EscapeString("")`),
+    and a guard's variable too: write a tautology as `(x == recorded || true)` or `(!held[p] || true)`,
+    not by deleting the compare (five such first drafts failed "declared and not used" in 86bctmuwy),
+    keep the failed receipt as NOT A KILL and supersede it with a versioned
+    variant (`M13b-v2`) that builds. (2026-10-23, 901u v2 builder.)
+14. **A negative fixture that drops two fields hides the second guard.** If a
+    "missing id" case also drops the type, the earlier type guard answers and
+    deleting the id guard survives. Vary one field per negative case, and rebuild
+    fixture folders for every case: a hard link made in one case survives later
+    `>` writes and quietly couples the next case's "independent" files.
+    (2026-10-23: the empty-agent_id guard survived in both `~/.claude/hooks`
+    gate suites.)
+
+15. **A "largest wins" pick over ordered keys needs two fixtures**, the largest first and the largest last: with one,
+    the keep-first or keep-last mutant survives, and a tie case can kill it for the wrong reason (elementor-footer-fit,
+    2026-11-08).
+
+16. **A "wait while pending" guard is killed only by a case where the thing arrives inside the wait** (held 8 s under a 15 s cap): a held-past-the-cap case passes with or without the wait, and a fake sharing one counter across retried loads hides a no-wait mutant (staging-fit-capture, 2026-11-09).
+
+17. **A "stays still" check that reads the end state after a wait passes on a looping thing that never paused** when the wait is a whole number of its cycles (3 slides × 900 ms read after 2.7 s): count the events during the wait and add a control that it moves again afterwards (site-slider, 2026-11-09).
+
+18. **A value looked up per member of a set** (a stand-in box per width, a rule per tier) needs a fixture whose value differs across the set and a test line asserting it differs, or the mutant "the first member's value for every member" survives (site-reviews, 2026-11-09).
 
